              "target": "/workspace/eco-auditor (package-lock.json dependency tree)",
              "impact": "Depending on the CVE: unauthenticated denial of service against the application's routing layer, open redirects that enable phishing from the trusted ecoauditor.io domain, information disclosure of route constructor details, path traversal during the build (postcss source maps), and WebSocket memory-exhaustion DoS where ws is used. Open-redirect and DoS issues in react-router are directly reachable in the deployed single-page application.",
              "technical_analysis": "trivy fs scan of the repository's package-lock.json reports: body-parser 1.20.5 (LOW, fix 1.20.6/2.3.0), esbuild 0.27.7 (LOW, fix 0.28.1 — note package.json already overrides esbuild to 0.28.0 but the lock still resolves 0.27.7 in a path), postcss 8.5.14 (HIGH, fix 8.5.18; package.json pins exactly 8.5.14), react-router 7.17.0 (HIGH DoS CVE-2026-55685 + HIGH RSC CSRF GHSA-qwww-vcr4-c8h2 + 3 MEDIUM incl. open redirect; fix 7.18.0/8.3.0), ws 8.20.1 (HIGH, fix 8.21.0). Root cause: exact/pinned versions in package.json (postcss 8.5.14) and stale transitive ranges (react-router ^7.14.0 resolving to 7.17.0) without routine lockfile updates.",
              "remediation_steps": "1. Upgrade react-router to >=7.18.0 (or 8.3.0 if adopting v8) and regenerate package-lock.json. 2. Bump the pinned postcss from 8.5.14 to >=8.5.18 in package.json. 3. Upgrade ws to >=8.21.0 and body-parser to >=1.20.6 (express ^4.22.1 chain) via lockfile refresh. 4. Pin esbuild to the fixed 0.28.1+ (existing override only needs a patch bump). 5. Add npm audit / trivy fs to CI with a severity gate (fail on HIGH) and enable Dependabot/Renovate for routine updates. 6. Re-run trivy fs after upgrades and confirm zero HIGH findings.",
              "poc": {
                "description": "1. Run trivy fs --scanners vuln against the repository: it reports 9 vulnerabilities in package-lock.json with CVE/GHSA identifiers and fixed versions (output preserved in the assessment artifacts). 2. Verify installed versions: react-router 7.17.0, postcss 8.5.14, ws 8.20.1 in the lockfile. 3. Cross-reference each identifier with its published advisory (e.g. GHSA-r28c-9q8g-f849 postcss source-map path traversal; CVE-2026-55685 react-router route-matching DoS).",
